sendmailanalyzer (10.0.16-6) stable; urgency=high

  * Replace per-member `tar -xOzf` legacy archive reads with a staged archive
    cache: each monthly `history.tar.gz` is expanded once for only the selected
    `.dat` members and released after its final imported entry.
  * Import each legacy host/day inside one SQLite transaction instead of
    committing every INSERT/UPDATE independently, drastically reducing WAL and
    filesystem write amplification during historical migration.
  * Print archive-extraction and per-day commit progress so package upgrades no
    longer appear hung while importing substantial 9.4 histories.
  * Bound temporary extraction disk usage by deleting each staged archive cache
    as soon as its last selected entry has been consumed; source archives and
    the active v10 SQLite database remain untouched until final validation.
  * Retain the Queue-ID generation disambiguation, full `history.tar.gz` import,
    Apache multi-vhost migration, exact audit, quick-check, rollback database,
    and postinst service-state recovery from 10.0.16-5.

